{
 "source": "frames_cosmetic_b.png",
 "notes": [
  "S4b: the six portrait frames frames_cosmetic_a.json did not paint (docs/art/PAINTING_BRIEFS.md 1.13; balance/cosmetics.json `art`: frames/<id>) -- Companion's, the Thirtieth, Loyal Vassal (the calendar's day 14), Rising Lord (Victory Road, level 20), Heir (the guide's end) and the Royal Charter -- each painted as a square (left) and a ring (right) on the sheet's flat navy, keyed off it exactly as sheet a's are (darkkey against [9,19,29], k 38, floor 4); the EMPTY windows key clear.",
  "Sheet a's scales, so the two sheets are one set: every square at 0.6324 (a plain band 160 across: Companion's and Loyal Vassal's measure 251 and 252 painted, sheet a's 250-252) and every ring at 0.4167 (its window, 83-86 in radius on both sheets, comes out the same; this sheet paints its rings' bands thinner, so they are a little smaller outside). _tile is the ring whole in the wardrobe's 224x190 art box; looks/<id>_ring_large (looks.json) the same ring at sheet a's 0.5697.",
  "Each crop is centred on its frame's own window -- a square's from its inner edges along the centre lines clear of the middle ornaments, a ring's from a circle fitted to its inner edge on the diagonals -- and masked to a polygon round that frame's own ink (the component against the ground, grown 3 px): the Loyal Vassal's key hangs into the Rising Lord's rays, and each would carry the other's otherwise. Written by a measuring script (the W3-calendar fork's scratchpad gen_frames_b.py): its numbers, not hand-read ones."
 ],
